Title: Shared census model-ordering function (heatmap vs Figure 2 drift)
Created: 2026-06-09
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-06-09T20:29Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Two Exp1 figures order the same 14-model census but compute the order with
two different rules, so they can silently disagree:

- **Figure 2** (`fig_direct_p1_base`, `plot_method_convergence.write_pdf`)
  sorts by `(model_family, -_model_size_b(model, size_class), model)`.
  `_model_size_b` resolves the confirmed parameter-count registry
  `_KNOWN_SIZE_B` (→ regex on the name → `size_class` fallback). It reads
  `size_class` from the measurement records.
- **Figure 4** (`fig_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1`,
  `plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.heatmap_models`) sorts by
  `(model_family, -_model_size_rank(model), model)`. `_model_size_rank`
  (from `plot_quality_spider_exp1`) is a coarse name-substring tier
  (haiku/small/20b/flash→1, sonnet/medium/35b/120b/plus→2,
  opus/large/max/pro/5.5→3). It reads only the model name, because the
  heatmap's input (`experiments/derived/exp1_cross_eval.csv`) has no
  `size_class` column.

For the current cohort the two orders agree — but only via the alphabetical
final tiebreak, and the tier heuristic is brittle: a future model whose name
dodges every tier keyword lands in the default tier (2) and the figures
diverge. PR #914 added `test_model_order_literal_matches_figure2_render` as a
tripwire (a hardcoded 14-name list verified against the committed Figure 2
PDF), which catches a regression but does **not** give the two figures a
single source of truth to fix it in one place.

This was raised in the #914 Copilot review (the docstrings/caption were
softened from "effective parameter size descending / identical to Figure 2"
to "approximation, verified for this cohort"). The honest wording is shipped;
this ticket removes the underlying duplication.

## Goal

One canonical ordering function both figures call, name-resolvable (works
without `size_class`), with the parameter registry as the single source of
truth.

## Approach (guidance, not binding)

- Extract `census_model_order(models: Iterable[str]) -> list[str]` — likely
  next to `_model_size_b` in `plot_method_convergence`, or in `util` if that
  pulls in no heavy deps. Key: `(model_family(m), -size_b(m), m)`.
- Make size resolution work from the **name alone** so the heatmap can use it:
  `_model_size_b(model, size_class=None)` already falls back to the regex and
  then the `size_class` default (500). Add the 6 exp1 models missing confirmed
  sizes to `_KNOWN_SIZE_B` (claude-haiku-4.5 / -sonnet-4.6 / -opus-4.6,
  gpt-5.5, deepseek-v4-pro / -flash, qwen3.7-max, qwen3.6-flash) so the
  name-only path orders them correctly instead of colliding at 500.
  **Caution:** `_KNOWN_SIZE_B` is checked *before* `size_class` in
  `_model_size_b`, so any value added here also changes Figure 2's order if it
  disagrees with the current `size_class`-derived size. Pin the added values to
  reproduce today's Figure 2 order (regression-guard below).
- Repoint `heatmap_models` and `plot_method_convergence`'s inline sort at the
  shared function. Delete `_model_size_rank` if nothing else uses it
  (`plot_quality_spider_exp1` still does for its 2x2 panels — check before
  removing; it may stay for the spider only).

## First test (write before code)

```python
# tests/test_census_model_order.py
def test_heatmap_and_figure2_share_one_order():
    """The heatmap and Figure 2 produce identical column/row order via the
    shared census_model_order — not two heuristics that happen to agree."""
    from aedist.plot_method_convergence import census_model_order
    from aedist.plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1 import heatmap_models
    from aedist.plot_quality_spider_exp1 import _load_rows

    rows = _load_rows("experiments/derived/exp1_cross_eval.csv")
    models = sorted({r["model"].strip() for r in rows if r["model"].strip()})
    assert heatmap_models(rows) == census_model_order(models)
    # And it still matches the visually-verified literal from PR #914.
    assert census_model_order(models) == [
        "claude-opus-4.6", "claude-sonnet-4.6", "claude-haiku-4.5",
        "deepseek-v4-pro", "deepseek-v4-flash", "gpt-5.5",
        "gpt-oss-120b", "gpt-oss-20b", "mistral-large-2512",
        "mistral-medium-3-5", "mistral-small-2603", "qwen3.7-max",
        "qwen3.6-35b-a3b", "qwen3.6-flash",
    ]
```

## Definition of done

- [ ] `census_model_order` exists in one module; `heatmap_models` and
      `plot_method_convergence` both call it (no second size heuristic for
      census ordering).
- [ ] Size resolution works from the model name alone (heatmap path needs no
      `size_class`); the 6 missing exp1 models are in `_KNOWN_SIZE_B` with
      values pinned to preserve today's Figure 2 order.
- [ ] `test_census_model_order.py` (the first test above) passes; the PR #914
      literal-order test is folded into / superseded by it (no orphaned
      duplicate).
- [ ] Both `fig_direct_p1_base.pdf` and `fig_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.pdf`
      rebuild byte-for-deterministically with unchanged model order (visual
      diff = none).
- [ ] `_model_size_rank` either deleted (if unused) or documented as
      spider-only; no dead import.
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/plot_method_convergence.py` — `_model_size_b`, `_KNOWN_SIZE_B`, inline census sort
- `src/aedist/plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.py` — `heatmap_models`
- `src/aedist/plot_quality_spider_exp1.py` — `_model_size_rank` (other consumer)
- `tests/test_plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.py` — `test_model_order_literal_matches_figure2_render` (to fold in)

## Priority

Low — maintainability cleanup, not a correctness bug. Current behaviour is
correct and tripwire-guarded by #914. Pick up post-arXiv.
